FINDING (non-blocking, no acceptance criterion and no repo gate covers it):
  gofmt regression in internal/models/transaction.go. `gofmt -l internal/models/
  internal/services/dataloader/` lists it; `gofmt -l` on `git show
  HEAD:internal/models/transaction.go` lists NOTHING, so HEAD was clean and
  this change made it unclean. Cause: the new doc comment splits the struct's
  alignment group, so gofmt wants ID/Date/Amount/Description dealigned and
  OriginalDescription's tag aligned to the second group (`gofmt -d` output).
  loader_test.go is also gofmt-unclean but was ALREADY unclean at HEAD, so that
  one is not a regression. I searched for an enforcing gate
  (`grep -rn gofmt swarm/ Makefile .github`, and IMPORT_FIXES_SPEC.md) and found
  none, so this does not fail any written criterion. One `gofmt -w` fixes it.

Scope of my own actions: I edited nothing. The only scratch artefacts were in
/tmp/.../scratchpad, including a detached git worktree at HEAD which I removed
(`git worktree remove --force`; `git worktree list` shows only the repo, and
`git status --porcelain` afterwards shows the same modified set as before).
